            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To multiply powers of the same base, we add the exponents:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2^2\\times 2^{-5} =2^{2+(-5)} = 2^{-3}]</span></p><p>To evaluate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2^{-3},]</span> we find the reciprocal of the base <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (2)]</span> and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the opposite sign:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2^{-3}  = \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^3 =\\dfrac{1}{2} \\times \\dfrac{1}{2} \\times \\dfrac{1}{2} = \\dfrac{1}{8}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "To multiply powers of the same base, we add the exponents:\n[MATH: 2^2\\times 2^{-5} =2^{2+(-5)} = 2^{-3}]\n\nTo evaluate [MATH: 2^{-3},] we find the reciprocal of the base [MATH: (2)] and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the opposite sign:\n\n[MATH: 2^{-3} = \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^3 =\\dfrac{1}{2} \\times \\dfrac{1}{2} \\times \\dfrac{1}{2} = \\dfrac{1}{8}]",
            "images": [],
